WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.549
<c.running>Episode 1 is the night the whole axis is</c>

2
00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:09.234
<c.running>counted from: by our working convention, Y0.</c>

3
00:00:09.619 --> 00:00:11.569
<c.steel>Aaron asked for a thirty-minute oil</c>

4
00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:14.147
<c.steel>paint-along of his own two characters,</c>

5
00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.150
<c.steel>Jefrie and BloodTailor,</c>

6
00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.665
<c.steel>with four voices who never</c>

7
00:00:17.665 --> 00:00:19.761
<c.steel>introduce themselves.</c>

8
00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:22.746
<c.fact>For twenty minutes a gentle painter teaches</c>

9
00:00:22.746 --> 00:00:26.844
<c.fact>real oil craft: value, edges, wet-in-wet,</c>

10
00:00:26.844 --> 00:00:30.008
<c.fact>glazing, fat over lean.</c>

11
00:00:30.384 --> 00:00:33.043
<c.fact>Then the bell tolls, the side bars slide</c>

12
00:00:33.043 --> 00:00:36.184
<c.fact>away, and the painting fills the screen.</c>

13
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.453
<c.fact>After that it is flown over,</c>

14
00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:42.168
<c.fact>X-rayed, cut back, sung, filmed silent,</c>

15
00:00:42.168 --> 00:00:45.541
<c.fact>over-painted, hung and relit.</c>

16
00:00:46.827 --> 00:00:51.065
<c.fact>The host is never seen: no face, no hands,</c>

17
00:00:51.065 --> 00:00:55.993
<c.fact>only his brush, his voice and the subtitles.</c>

18
00:00:56.387 --> 00:00:59.034
<c.steel>Aaron cast him as a homage to a famous</c>

19
00:00:59.034 --> 00:01:00.718
<c.steel>public-television painter;</c>

20
00:01:00.718 --> 00:01:02.947
<c.running>and as a working rule he is never</c>

21
00:01:02.947 --> 00:01:06.157
<c.running>named and never impersonated.</c>

22
00:01:06.547 --> 00:01:08.915
<c.fact>Paintings speak to him, and he</c>

23
00:01:08.915 --> 00:01:11.371
<c.fact>answers with total courtesy,</c>

24
00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.751
<c.fact>as if it happens all the time.</c>

25
00:01:13.977 --> 00:01:16.125
<c.fact>He gives the last stroke away,</c>

26
00:01:16.125 --> 00:01:18.993
<c.fact>and his last clean word, said softly</c>

27
00:01:18.993 --> 00:01:22.726
<c.fact>to the viewer, is Goodnight.</c>

28
00:01:23.108 --> 00:01:26.196
<c.running>By our running reading, every calm one after</c>

29
00:01:26.196 --> 00:01:30.329
<c.running>him rhymes him: Teo, the agent and the chess</c>

30
00:01:30.329 --> 00:01:33.528
<c.running>teacher, each ending on Goodnight.</c>

31
00:01:34.822 --> 00:01:37.144
<c.steel>Jefrie is Aaron's own character,</c>

32
00:01:37.144 --> 00:01:40.499
<c.steel>set in steel: a small young warrior girl</c>

33
00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:43.663
<c.steel>from the same dark world as BloodTailor.</c>

34
00:01:44.042 --> 00:01:47.188
<c.steel>But Aaron has also said that Episode 1's</c>

35
00:01:47.188 --> 00:01:49.998
<c.steel>Jefrie is not actually going to be canon</c>

36
00:01:49.998 --> 00:01:54.695
<c.steel>Jefrie: her lines are only what Jefrie would say.</c>

37
00:01:55.091 --> 00:01:57.285
<c.fact>Inside the painting she is silent</c>

38
00:01:57.285 --> 00:01:59.323
<c.fact>until the rag gives her a mouth,</c>

39
00:01:59.422 --> 00:02:01.488
<c.fact>and her first remark is about the</c>

40
00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:04.646
<c.fact>host's first story: she has been</c>

41
00:02:04.646 --> 00:02:07.276
<c.fact>listening since the start.</c>

42
00:02:07.656 --> 00:02:09.212
<c.fact>She tells the painter to make her</c>

43
00:02:09.212 --> 00:02:11.795
<c.fact>tail heavier, and she is right.</c>

44
00:02:12.207 --> 00:02:14.785
<c.running>By our running reading, she never returns</c>

45
00:02:14.785 --> 00:02:17.722
<c.running>as cast: only as a painting,</c>

46
00:02:17.722 --> 00:02:21.606
<c.running>a print, a drawing or a sound.</c>

47
00:02:22.896 --> 00:02:24.870
<c.fact>At four forty-seven in the morning,</c>

48
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.437
<c.fact>a caller rings in,</c>

49
00:02:26.437 --> 00:02:29.258
<c.fact>painting along since the 2 a.m. airing,</c>

50
00:02:29.258 --> 00:02:31.789
<c.fact>for his little sister: it's for my</c>

51
00:02:31.789 --> 00:02:35.592
<c.fact>sister, Rosie. She's nine today.</c>

52
00:02:35.982 --> 00:02:40.087
<c.fact>He counts things, the bell, the days,</c>

53
00:02:40.185 --> 00:02:43.813
<c.fact>the seconds, and he is usually right:</c>

54
00:02:44.039 --> 00:02:46.036
<c.fact>he predicts the last stroke</c>

55
00:02:46.036 --> 00:02:49.003
<c.fact>at exactly twenty minutes.</c>

56
00:02:49.382 --> 00:02:52.767
<c.fact>At five-oh-nine, Rosie's painting is done:</c>

57
00:02:52.935 --> 00:02:56.203
<c.fact>attempt number four, on a pizza-box lid.</c>

58
00:02:56.302 --> 00:02:59.245
<c.fact>Then he falls asleep on the line.</c>

59
00:03:00.522 --> 00:03:02.856
<c.fact>The pitchman shouts in capitals,</c>

60
00:03:02.856 --> 00:03:05.851
<c.fact>prices everything, and owns the phrase</c>

61
00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:09.085
<c.fact>BUT WAIT, which the host bans.</c>

62
00:03:09.497 --> 00:03:11.459
<c.steel>Aaron cast him as a homage</c>

63
00:03:11.459 --> 00:03:14.286
<c.steel>to a famous TV pitchman.</c>

64
00:03:14.679 --> 00:03:16.873
<c.fact>He has carried a one-hair brush for</c>

65
00:03:16.873 --> 00:03:19.747
<c.fact>eleven years and never got it wet.</c>

66
00:03:20.054 --> 00:03:23.056
<c.fact>That night it makes the last stroke:</c>

67
00:03:23.282 --> 00:03:25.767
<c.fact>a catch-light in Jefrie's eye,</c>

68
00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:28.257
<c.fact>with nobody holding it.</c>

69
00:03:29.554 --> 00:03:32.573
<c.fact>Eleven minutes in, the host paints a small</c>

70
00:03:32.573 --> 00:03:35.922
<c.fact>cabin with one lit window into the ruins,</c>

71
00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.497
<c.fact>and says only: there, that one's just for me.</c>

72
00:03:40.723 --> 00:03:44.433
<c.fact>Three strokes of gold paint it out.</c>

73
00:03:44.809 --> 00:03:48.269
<c.fact>After the turn, an X-ray finds it, and its</c>

74
00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:51.270
<c.fact>window is the only warm pixel on the plate.</c>

75
00:03:51.369 --> 00:03:54.312
<c.fact>He says: I always put one in.</c>

76
00:03:54.817 --> 00:03:57.691
<c.fact>Usually it's the part you paint over.</c>

77
00:03:58.078 --> 00:04:00.963
<c.egg>It is the series' longest-running egg.</c>

78
00:04:01.189 --> 00:04:04.795
<c.egg>Teo draws a one-window cabin and rubs it out,</c>

79
00:04:04.893 --> 00:04:07.401
<c.egg>Episode 3's agent is a cursor</c>

80
00:04:07.401 --> 00:04:09.102
<c.egg>the colour of that window,</c>

81
00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.700
<c.egg>and in Episode 4 only the colour is left.</c>

82
00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:17.962
<c.open>Why he puts one in is still open.</c>

83
00:04:19.247 --> 00:04:21.615
<c.steel>Behind them stands the Storm Bell:</c>

84
00:04:21.615 --> 00:04:25.035
<c.steel>in Aaron's own canon, Jefrie's home.</c>

85
00:04:25.342 --> 00:04:27.490
<c.fact>In Episode 1 it tolls every five</c>

86
00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.615
<c.fact>minutes, and nobody mentions it until</c>

87
00:04:29.615 --> 00:04:31.989
<c.fact>the caller counts three.</c>

88
00:04:32.386 --> 00:04:34.604
<c.fact>Its fourth toll breaks the broadcast</c>

89
00:04:34.604 --> 00:04:36.351
<c.fact>window at twenty minutes.</c>

90
00:04:36.519 --> 00:04:39.665
<c.egg>Later nights bury it: re-pitched to F</c>

91
00:04:39.665 --> 00:04:42.278
<c.egg>under every chat chime in Episode 2,</c>

92
00:04:42.278 --> 00:04:44.797
<c.egg>and to A under Rosie's check-ins</c>

93
00:04:44.797 --> 00:04:47.032
<c.egg>in Episode 3.</c>

94
00:04:47.432 --> 00:04:51.449
<c.idea>One idea on the table: D, F and A walk a</c>

95
00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:54.735
<c.idea>D minor chord, and a later episode might</c>

96
00:04:54.735 --> 00:04:58.085
<c.idea>ring it on D again, at twenty minutes.</c>

97
00:04:59.381 --> 00:05:01.517
<c.open>The first night leaves a lot open on</c>

98
00:05:01.517 --> 00:05:05.691
<c.open>purpose. Nobody knows whose room the end room is.</c>

99
00:05:05.999 --> 00:05:08.257
<c.open>The caller's name is unknown,</c>

100
00:05:08.425 --> 00:05:10.637
<c.open>and so is what became of him.</c>

101
00:05:10.945 --> 00:05:13.011
<c.open>And how Rosie knew about the girl with</c>

102
00:05:13.011 --> 00:05:15.275
<c.open>the tail, nineteen hours before the</c>

103
00:05:15.275 --> 00:05:17.743
<c.open>broadcast, is still open.</c>

104
00:05:18.136 --> 00:05:20.621
<c.open>Even whether the show was live is open:</c>

105
00:05:20.621 --> 00:05:25.027
<c.open>the caller asks, and gets only, hi, friend.</c>

106
00:05:26.323 --> 00:05:28.529
<c.running>By our running count, Episode 2's</c>

107
00:05:28.529 --> 00:05:31.821
<c.running>film quotes this night twelve times,</c>

108
00:05:31.919 --> 00:05:34.758
<c.running>and Episode 3's twenty-five.</c>

109
00:05:35.065 --> 00:05:39.994
Next: sixty years on, a city for the Moon.
